   "claims": [
    "This tool uses 2026 tax brackets and the updated W-4 form to provide highly accurate estimates.",
    "You can also use it to help you confidently fill out Steps 3 and 4 of your W-4.",
    "Common examples include health insurance premiums, 401(k) retirement contributions, health savings account (HSA) funding, union dues, and mandated child support payments.",
    "For the 2026 tax year, the standard deduction is set at $16,100 for single filers and $32,200 for married couples filing jointly.",
    "For the 2026 tax year, the top marginal federal income tax rate is 37%.",
    "California has one of the highest top marginal state tax rates, at 13.30%.",
    "New Hampshire and Tennessee also do not tax earned wages; New Hampshire's tax on interest and dividend income was repealed effective 2025, and Tennessee's ended in 2021.",
    "FICA is automatically deducted from a portion of your gross wages, regardless of whether you are a standard W-2 employee or an independent contractor.",
    "The employee Social Security tax rate is 6.20% (bringing the combined employee-employer total to 12.40%).",
    "Medicare Medicare is a single-payer federal health insurance program in the United States designed primarily for citizens aged 65 and older."
   ],
